---
import PageLayout from '@micro/ui/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  site={site}
  title={`About | ${site.name}`}
  description="About the free Working Days Calculator: what it does, where its public holiday data comes from, and how it handles your data."
  path="/about/"
  heading="About the Working Days Calculator"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <p>
    The Working Days Calculator is a free, simple tool for counting business days between two dates and for adding or
    subtracting business days from a date. It is made for everyday tasks such as working out deadlines, notice
    periods, delivery estimates and project schedules.
  </p>
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Counts working days between two dates, with the option to include the end date.</li>
    <li>Adds or subtracts working days from a date.</li>
    <li>Includes public holidays for 14 countries, with states and regions where available.</li>
    <li>Supports Saturday–Sunday, Friday–Saturday, Sunday-only and custom weekends.</li>
    <li>Lets you untick holidays and add your own days off.</li>
    <li>Saves your inputs in the page address so you can share a result.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The calculator runs entirely in your browser. There are no accounts, and your dates are not sent to a server. See
    the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
  </p>
  <h2>Holiday data and credits</h2>
  <p>
    Public holiday rules come from the open-source
    <a href="https://github.com/commenthol/date-holidays">date-holidays</a> project by commenthol and contributors. The
    holiday data is based on Wikipedia articles and is available under
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>; the code is available under the ISC
    licence. We use the data as published and do not add or change holidays.
  </p>
  <p>
    Holiday dates can change, and regional, industry or company holidays may not be included. If you spot a mistake,
    please <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
